    "question": "A company has implemented a new security requirement. According to the new requirement, the company must scan all tra c from corporate AWS instances in the company's VPC for violations of the company's security policies. As a result of these scans, the company can block access to and from speci c IP addresses. To meet the new requirement, the company deploys a set of Amazon EC2 instances in private subnets to serve as transparent proxies. The company installs approved proxy server software on these EC2 instances. The company modi es the route tables on all subnets to use the corresponding EC2 instances with proxy software as the default route. The company also creates security groups that are compliant with the security policies and assigns these security groups to the EC2 instances. Despite these configurations, the tra c of the EC2 instances in their private subnets is not being properly forwarded to the internet. What should a solutions architect do to resolve this issue?",
    "question_zh": "一家公司提出新的安全要求：扫描公司 VPC 内所有 AWS 实例的流量，检查是否违反安全策略，并能阻断发往或来自特定 IP 地址的流量。公司在私有子网部署一组 EC2 实例作为透明代理，安装批准的代理软件，将所有子网的默认路由指向相应代理实例，并为实例配置符合策略的安全组。完成这些配置后，私有子网实例的流量仍未正确转发到互联网。架构师应如何解决？",
